  "definition": "Lambert & Burgard 2025 Eq. 1-3 with REF/+1/+2 = Tbot 0.0/1.0/2.0; M = shelf-mean melt (m a-1); final-fold model of each method (in-sample at 0.0 and 1.0, test at 2.0); DA_p1_p2 is Eq. 3 applied to the (+1, +2) interval (extension)",
  "caveat": "REF (Tbot 0.0) and +1 (1.0) are IN-SAMPLE maps of the final-fold model (trained on those runs); only +2 (Tbot 2.0) is held out. For the flexible methods (M4-M7) the REF/+1 values largely reproduce the training data, so dM/dT|(REF,+1) and DA_ref_p1 are not an independent test of learned sensitivity, and dM/dT|(+1,+2) restates the final-test error. DA_p1_p2 is an extension of LB25 Eq. 3 (defined over REF,+1 only). DA flagged *_small_denominator where |dM/dT| < 0.5 m a-1 degC-1 (post hoc display rule): a ratio of small numbers, e.g. M4 at z_c = 550, DA_ref_p1 = 25.4 with dM/dT = 0.36, a small-denominator artefact.",
  "da_small_denominator_threshold": 0.5
